{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Not found
  Phase 10. The surface every mistyped URL, dead link, deleted product and
  shared sold-out URL lands on.

  Sources of truth:
  - PHASE-1-WEBSITE-AUDIT.md SHOP-09, which lists 404 among the templates
    Shopify serves and this theme had never designed, and records that Shopify
    returns an error page for any storefront route whose template is missing.
  - PHASE-2-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §8 (the container model), §10.1 (the accent
    variant lives on dark surfaces only).
  - snippets/cart-empty-state.liquid, for the destination decision below.

  THE DEFAULT DESTINATION IS THE HOME PAGE, NOT A COLLECTION.
  This is the same "where do we send them" question the empty cart already
  answered, and the answer does not change because the dead end is a URL rather
  than an empty cart. cart-empty-state.liquid records the reason:
  routes.all_products_collection_url is the obvious answer and it is wrong here,
  because it depends on a collection template this theme has not always had —
  and sending a customer who has just hit one error page to a second one is the
  worst outcome this file can produce. The home page exists unconditionally.
  The merchant can point the button anywhere, which is what the url setting is
  for, and is how this resolves the day a collection template ships.

  THE COPY IS GENERIC UI COPY, NOT BRAND COPY.
  The heading and the message are locale strings, not brand voice: nothing here
  is a tagline, a scripture, a joke about being lost, or a claim of any kind.
  The button label is the one merchant-editable string and it carries no schema
  default, so an untouched theme keeps reading the label out of
  locales/en.default.json — a schema default would freeze one language into
  settings_data.json and every other locale would render English.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE.
  No search form: the header already carries the store's search control on this
  page like every other, and a second one would be a duplicate of a control the
  customer can see. No product recommendations and no "you might like" row —
  there is no data behind either and inventing one is invention. No list of
  suggested destinations, because every destination in this project is
  BUSINESS INFORMATION REQUIRED (Phase 1 Appendix A) and the merchant's menu in
  the header is the supported answer. No automatic redirect: URL redirects are
  a Shopify admin feature, and a client-side one takes the address bar away
  from someone who may simply have mistyped one character.

  ZERO JavaScript.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign back_url = section.settings.button_url
  if back_url == blank
    assign back_url = routes.root_url
  endif

  assign back_label = section.settings.button_label | strip
  if back_label == blank
    assign back_label = 'general.not_found.link' | t
  endif
-%}

{{ 'section-main-404.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  surface-dark is fixed rather than a setting. Phase 2 §10.1 gives the accent
  variant no light-surface rule at all, so the one call to action on this page
  paints only on ink — and §9 of the house conventions limits a main-* section
  to the decisions a merchant actually has, which here is where the button
  goes, not what colour the page is.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="main-404 surface-dark" {{ section.shopify_attributes }}>
  <div class="main-404__inner container">
    <h1 class="main-404__title">{{ 'general.not_found.title' | t }}</h1>
    <p class="main-404__body">{{ 'general.not_found.body' | t }}</p>

    <a class="button button--accent main-404__action" href="{{ back_url }}">
      {{ back_label }}
      {% render 'icon-arrow' %}
    </a>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Not found",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "main-404-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "button_url",
      "label": "Where the button goes",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the home page, which is the same default the empty cart uses. Point it at a collection only once that collection's page is working, or this page sends people to a second error. If you change it, change the button label below too — the default label names the home page."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "info": "Leave empty to use the theme's own wording, which is translated with the rest of the store. Anything typed here replaces it in every language."
    }
  ],
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["404"]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
